    <h1>Deterministic Scale: Architecture of Fault-Tolerant Distributed Ledgers</h1>
    <p>By Dr. Vikramaditya Rao | ISBN: 978-81-974021-2-1</p>
  </header>
  <main>
    <section><h2>Chapter 1: Why At-Least-Once Delivery Requires Idempotent Sinks</h2><p>Every external webhook is a potentially duplicated message. Treating an incoming payment notification as an blind append operation guarantees eventual double-fulfillment. Instead, an idempotent sink records the provider's unique event identifier inside the same atomic boundary that transitions the order state.</p></section>
<section><h2>Chapter 2: Constant-Time Cryptographic Verification</h2><p>Before parsing a single field of a webhook payload for business logic, verify the HMAC-SHA256 digest computed over the exact raw byte stream using constant-time byte comparison.</p></section>
  </main>
